WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:14.726
Ethan's stomach was growling.

2
00:00:14.727 --> 00:00:20.505
He had been hungry all day, even after eating lunch.

3
00:00:20.506 --> 00:00:23.221
Mr. Dunn clapped his hands.

4
00:00:23.222 --> 00:00:25.415
"All right, campers.

5
00:00:25.416 --> 00:00:30.844
Let's clean up and head outside."

6
00:00:30.845 --> 00:00:37.480
The kids put away their art things and followed Mr. Dunn outside.

7
00:00:37.481 --> 00:00:41.384
"You've all played tic-tac-toe, right?" he said.

8
00:00:41.385 --> 00:00:43.306
Everyone nodded.

9
00:00:43.307 --> 00:00:46.696
"And normally you play on paper, right?"

10
00:00:46.697 --> 00:00:49.030
Everyone nodded again.

11
00:00:49.031 --> 00:00:55.761
"Well, today we will play a 3-D version of tic-tac-toe."

12
00:00:55.762 --> 00:00:59.477
"What does 3-D mean?" Nina asked.

13
00:00:59.478 --> 00:01:04.971
"It's when something isn't flat like a drawing on a piece of paper," Jason explained.

14
00:01:04.972 --> 00:01:12.274
"If something has height, width, and depth, it's three-dimensional, or 3-D. Like us!"

15
00:01:12.275 --> 00:01:15.115
"Right," Mr. Dunn said.

16
00:01:15.116 --> 00:01:22.425
"Today instead of drawing X's and O's for tic-tac-toe, you'll toss beanbags."

17
00:01:22.426 --> 00:01:25.127
He showed them the beanbags.

18
00:01:25.128 --> 00:01:28.255
They were lumpy sacks tied at the top.

19
00:01:28.256 --> 00:01:33.603
"The blue ones have X's on them, and the white ones have O's."

20
00:01:33.604 --> 00:01:36.839
"Did you make those?" Izzie asked.

21
00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:41.869
Mr. Dunn smiled. "Yes, I did. Last night."

22
00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:47.729
Izzie nodded. "They look homemade."

23
00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:51.691
"What's in them?" Ethan wanted to know.

24
00:01:51.692 --> 00:01:56.154
"We'll find out at the end of the game," said Mr. Dunn.

25
00:01:56.155 --> 00:01:58.958
"Now who wants to play first?"

26
00:01:58.959 --> 00:02:02.014
Bobby and Izzie raised their hands.

27
00:02:02.015 --> 00:02:12.405
"Okay, you two, stand behind this line.

28
00:02:12.406 --> 00:02:19.148
Bobby, you can be X, and Izzie, you'll be O."

29
00:02:19.149 --> 00:02:22.896
"You can go first," Bobby told Izzie.

30
00:02:22.897 --> 00:02:26.370
"Thanks," she said.

31
00:02:26.371 --> 00:02:30.251
She tossed her beanbag to the far-right corner of the board.

32
00:02:30.252 --> 00:02:32.352
Bobby went next.

33
00:02:32.353 --> 00:02:36.259
He tossed his bag to the space beneath her bag.

34
00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:40.442
Ethan noticed two more beanbags by Mr. Dunn's feet.

35
00:02:40.443 --> 00:02:43.891
"Are those extra beanbags?" he asked.

36
00:02:43.892 --> 00:02:48.617
Mr. Dunn nodded. "In case one gets ripped."

37
00:02:48.618 --> 00:02:50.962
He turned back to the board.

38
00:02:50.963 --> 00:02:54.961
"Nice play, Izzie!" he said, clapping.

39
00:02:54.962 --> 00:02:58.345
Izzie had gotten her three O's in a row.

40
00:02:58.346 --> 00:03:01.393
"I win!" she cried.

41
00:03:01.394 --> 00:03:04.168
"The winner gets to play again.

42
00:03:04.169 --> 00:03:08.092
Who wants to challenge Izzie?" Mr. Dunn asked.

43
00:03:08.093 --> 00:03:12.704
"I do!" said Jason.

44
00:03:12.705 --> 00:03:15.401
He stepped up to the line.

45
00:03:15.402 --> 00:03:18.426
"You can go first," Izzie said.

46
00:03:18.427 --> 00:03:21.116
"Since I'll probably win."

47
00:03:21.117 --> 00:03:25.579
Jason rolled his eyes and tossed his beanbag onto the board.

48
00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:29.715
Meanwhile Ethan picked up an extra beanbag.

49
00:03:29.716 --> 00:03:32.786
The beans inside felt a little soft.

50
00:03:32.787 --> 00:03:36.311
They were definitely not regular beans.

51
00:03:36.312 --> 00:03:39.073
Ethan sniffed the bag.

52
00:03:39.074 --> 00:03:41.790
"I knew it!" he thought.

53
00:03:41.791 --> 00:03:45.943
"Tic-tac-toe, three in a row!" Izzie cried.

54
00:03:45.944 --> 00:03:48.228
"Nina, it's your turn!"

55
00:03:48.229 --> 00:03:54.294
As Nina stepped up to the line, Ethan untied the beanbag.

56
00:03:54.295 --> 00:03:57.202
He emptied it into his mouth.

57
00:03:57.203 --> 00:04:00.319
"Oh no!" Nina cried.

58
00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:03.292
"This bag has a hole in it!"

59
00:04:03.293 --> 00:04:06.405
"Don't worry, we have extra bags.

60
00:04:06.406 --> 00:04:11.213
And no peeking at the filling yet, Nina," Mr. Dunn said.

61
00:04:11.214 --> 00:04:15.255
"Ethan, please toss me the extra O bag."

62
00:04:15.256 --> 00:04:18.852
Ethan looked at the empty beanbag in his hand.

63
00:04:18.853 --> 00:04:21.253
It had an O.

64
00:04:21.254 --> 00:04:24.745
"I can't, Mr. Dunn," said Ethan.

65
00:04:24.746 --> 00:04:28.224
"I ate all the beans inside!"

66
00:04:28.225 --> 00:04:31.788
"Ethan!" Mr. Dunn scolded him.

67
00:04:31.789 --> 00:04:34.471
"You didn't listen to me!"

68
00:04:34.472 --> 00:04:38.308
"But they were jelly beans!" Ethan said.

69
00:04:38.309 --> 00:04:42.154
"Delicious jelly beans!"

70
00:04:42.155 --> 00:04:46.135
"You ruined the game, Ethan!" Bobby said.

71
00:04:46.136 --> 00:04:49.354
"That's okay," Izzie said quickly.

72
00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:52.055
"Maybe it's time for a snack?"

73
00:04:52.056 --> 00:05:00.480
Mr. Dunn nodded. "Okay. Jelly beans for everyone."

74
00:05:00.481 --> 00:05:05.050
"Even Ethan?" asked Bobby.

75
00:05:05.051 --> 00:05:08.607
"Yes," Mr. Dunn said at last.

76
00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:17.538
He smiled. "Even Ethan!"

77
00:05:17.539 --> 00:05:35.112
[caption_out@
